    "abstract": "<jats:p>There are a number of strong associations between the regularity/complexity of urinary sex hormones (being formalized via fuzzy and distribution entropy) and vasomotor symptoms (VMS). Standardized metrics of hormonal regularity (i.e., hormonal entropy) show promise in being used to identify different hormonal profiles underlying VMS occurrence, to provide a general gauge of reproductive aging, and to help predict the overall character of VMS experiences for the remainder of the menopause transition and beyond.</jats:p>",
    "DOI": "10.1152/ajpendo.00083.2025",
